# clang-tidy configuration for the Silverdaw backend.
#
# This file is read when running `clang-tidy` from the command line (e.g.
# `scripts/Invoke-ClangTidy.ps1` or the VS Code task `backend: lint`).
# The IDE-time integration via clangd uses the separate `Diagnostics.ClangTidy`
# block in `.clangd`; both lists should be kept in sync.
#
# HeaderFilterRegex restricts diagnostics to *our* headers (under backend/src/)
# so we don't drown in warnings from JUCE / IXWebSocket / the C++ standard
# library, which are pulled in via target_link_libraries and won't be touched.
#
# The `-check` exclusions below are listed here with their reasons, because a
# block scalar cannot carry inline comments. A lint run is only useful if a
# warning means "look at this", so a check that fires by the hundred on a
# deliberate convention costs more than it finds: it buries the handful of real
# defects and trains everyone to ignore the output.
#
# THE BACKEND IS AT ZERO WARNINGS. Keep it there: fix what a run reports, or,
# if the check is genuinely wrong for this codebase, exclude it and add the
# reasoning below. An exclusion needs evidence, not a preference — for the
# bugprone-* entries here that meant reading every site the check flagged and
# establishing why it does not apply. Anything left unexplained is a warning
# waiting to be ignored.
#
#   readability-braces-around-statements   Single-line guard clauses
#       (`if (!x) return;`) are the house convention throughout the backend and
#       read better than a four-line block for an early exit.
#   readability-math-missing-parentheses   Demands parentheses around standard
#       operator precedence (`a - b / c`). Adds noise, not clarity.
#   readability-uppercase-literal-suffix   Wants `0.0F`; JUCE and this codebase
#       use lowercase `0.0f` everywhere.
#   modernize-use-auto                     Style preference. An explicit type is
#       often the more readable choice, especially for numeric and JUCE types.
#   modernize-use-nodiscard                Would demand `[[nodiscard]]` on
#       essentially every getter in the backend.
#   modernize-avoid-c-arrays               Fires on static lookup tables and on
#       JUCE interop, where a C array is the natural form.
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters   Fires on any two adjacent parameters
#       of the same type, which is unavoidable in audio code (gain/pan, in/out,
#       start/end). Noisy by design and not actionable.
#   bugprone-throwing-static-initialization Every hit is the
#       `static const juce::Identifier k…` idiom the ValueTree model is built on
#       (ADR 0002). Deliberate, pervasive, and not going to change.
#   readability-inconsistent-ifelse-braces Sibling of
#       readability-braces-around-statements above, and excluded for the same
#       reason: it re-flags the single-line guard clauses that are house style.
#   readability-isolate-declaration        Style preference for one declarator
#       per statement. `int x = 0, y = 0;` is fine and common in DSP loops.
#   readability-avoid-nested-conditional-operator  Nested ternaries in the
#       coefficient/curve maths are compact and local; expanding them into
#       if/else ladders makes the arithmetic harder to follow, not easier.
#   readability-implicit-bool-conversion   Fires on idiomatic JUCE and pointer
#       null-checks; the rewrite it wants is longer without being clearer.
#   readability-function-cognitive-complexity  A standing refactoring backlog
#       against ADR 0016, tracked there rather than re-reported on every run.
#       Excluded so a run of this lint means "something new needs attention".
#   performance-enum-size                  Wants `: std::uint8_t` on enums to
#       save 3 bytes per value. Bottom of the review priority order
#       (micro-optimisation) and it touches enums that appear in serialised
#       state, where the underlying type is not a free choice.
#   bugprone-misplaced-widening-cast       Every hit is `static_cast<size_t>`
#       of an FFT/stem bin index such as `2 * k`. Overflowing would need
#       k > 1e9 where the real bound is a few thousand. Checked, not real.
#   bugprone-exception-escape              The `juce::ThreadPool` job lambdas
#       it flags cannot terminate the process: JUCE wraps `runJob()` in
#       try/catch (see juce_ThreadPool.cpp). The rest are implicit destructors
#       of aggregates. Checked, not real.
#   bugprone-unchecked-optional-access     All hits are the member
#       `std::optional<Session> session` in ScratchSessionController. The
#       check's dataflow cannot carry a has-value fact across an intervening
#       member call (any of which might in principle `reset()` it), so it
#       re-flags helpers whose documented precondition is that the caller
#       holds sessionMutex and has already validated the session. Every call
#       site was audited and does exactly that. A class invariant the check
#       cannot see, not a missing check.
#   readability-use-anyofallof             Wants explicit loops rewritten as
#       std::any_of/all_of. With a lambda and iterator pair that is usually
#       longer than the loop it replaces; a style preference either way.
#   modernize-return-braced-init-list      Wants `return {arr};` in place of
#       `return juce::var(arr);`. Same reasoning as modernize-use-auto above:
#       naming the type being returned is the more readable choice, especially
#       for juce::var and juce::File, which have many constructors.
#   performance-no-automatic-move          Wants `const` dropped from locals
#       that are then returned, so the return can move rather than copy. The
#       types involved here are juce::String/juce::File, which are refcounted
#       — the "copy" is an atomic increment. Trading away a local's constness
#       for that is micro-optimisation, which is last in the review priority
#       order, and const-by-default is worth more than the increment.

---
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  readability-*,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -readability-braces-around-statements,
  -readability-math-missing-parentheses,
  -readability-uppercase-literal-suffix,
  -modernize-use-auto,
  -modernize-use-nodiscard,
  -modernize-avoid-c-arrays,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-throwing-static-initialization,
  -readability-inconsistent-ifelse-braces,
  -readability-isolate-declaration,
  -readability-avoid-nested-conditional-operator,
  -readability-implicit-bool-conversion,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity,
  -performance-enum-size,
  -bugprone-misplaced-widening-cast,
  -bugprone-exception-escape,
  -bugprone-unchecked-optional-access,
  -readability-use-anyofallof,
  -modernize-return-braced-init-list,
  -performance-no-automatic-move
WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*[\\/]backend[\\/]src[\\/].*'
FormatStyle: file
